            <div xml:id="d1232">

                <pb facs="1216" n="930" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg930"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 867.48/293</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Philip</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-03T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1916, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2678. Your 1821, May 21, and Department’s 2600, May 24.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1232-f1"/> Have you yet urged Ottoman Government to take steps for
                    protection Christians in Syria? For your information. Report from Cairo states
                    Syria famine-stricken, people dying starvation by thousands, particularly
                    Lebanon. Estimated 80,000 dead starvation Lebanon alone up to beginning May.
                    Also reported distress not due entirely natural war conditions, but to political
                    design on part Turkish Government to exterminate by starvation Christian
                    population. Eyewitnesses report military cordon prevents entry of food into
                    Lebanon. There is strong feeling of sympathy in the United States for destitute
                    in Syria, and many would like to send relief if this can be done. Ascertain
                    whether Turkish Government will permit relief supplies to be sent Lebanon and
                    other parts Syria, to be distributed by neutral committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
